{
  "name": "03c - Adapter: Approval Request",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 03c - Adapter: Approval Request\n\n**Swap point for the approver notification.**\n\nRenders the human-readable approval request (subject + body with\nthe exact curl the approver needs) and delivers it. Delivery is\nthe only part that is stubbed.\n\nDemo sink: Data Table `ap_notifications`. To go live, replace the\nsingle node `Deliver Approval Request`:\n\n| Target | Node |\n| --- | --- |\n| Email approver | Gmail -> Message -> Send |\n| Slack DM / channel | Slack -> Message -> Send |\n| Microsoft Teams | Microsoft Teams -> Message -> Send |\n| Approval app | HTTP Request -> POST /approvals |\n\n`Render Approval Notice` stays untouched in every case - the body\nit builds is channel-agnostic.",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 420,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "note-approval-adapter",
      "name": "Note: Approval Adapter",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -980,
        -340
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "inputSource": "workflowInputs",
        "workflowInputs": {
          "values": [
            {
              "name": "invoiceId",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "name": "vendor",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "name": "invoiceNumber",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "name": "currency",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "name": "total",
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "name": "confidence",
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "name": "holdReasons",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "name": "approveUrl",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "name": "recipient",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "name": "dueDate",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "when-called-by-pipeline",
      "name": "When Called by Pipeline",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -960,
        60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "const d = $json;\nlet reasons = [];\ntry { reasons = JSON.parse(d.holdReasons || '[]'); } catch (e) { reasons = [String(d.holdReasons || '')]; }\n\nconst money = `${d.currency} ${Number(d.total).toFixed(2)}`;\nconst subject = `AP approval needed: ${d.vendor} ${d.invoiceNumber} for ${money}`;\n\nconst body = [\n  `Invoice ${d.invoiceNumber} from ${d.vendor} needs your approval.`,\n  '',\n  `Amount    : ${money}`,\n  `Due date  : ${d.dueDate || 'not stated on the invoice'}`,\n  `Confidence: ${d.confidence}`,\n  `Invoice ID: ${d.invoiceId}`,\n  '',\n  'Why it was held:',\n  ...reasons.map((r) => `  - ${r}`),\n  '',\n  'Approve:',\n  `  curl -X POST ${d.approveUrl} -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\\`,\n  `    -d '{\"invoiceId\":\"${d.invoiceId}\",\"decision\":\"approve\",\"approver\":\"YOUR_NAME\"}'`,\n  '',\n  'Reject:',\n  `  curl -X POST ${d.approveUrl} -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\\`,\n  `    -d '{\"invoiceId\":\"${d.invoiceId}\",\"decision\":\"reject\",\"approver\":\"YOUR_NAME\",\"note\":\"why\"}'`,\n].join('\\n');\n\nreturn [{ json: { ...d, subject, body, channel: 'email', reasons } }];"
      },
      "id": "render-approval-notice",
      "name": "Render Approval Notice",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
